  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Two regular six-sided dice are rolled and the product of the numbers is recorded. Find the probability that the result is:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "greater than 2",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{11}{12}$",
          "worked": "There are $6\\times6=36$ equally likely ordered outcomes. The product is at most $2$ for $(1,1)$, $(1,2)$ and $(2,1)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{product}>2)&=1-\\frac{3}{36}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{product}>2)&=\\frac{11}{12}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "less than 30",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{11}{12}$",
          "worked": "There are $36$ equally likely ordered outcomes. The product is at least $30$ for $(5,6)$, $(6,5)$ and $(6,6)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{product}<30)&=1-\\frac{3}{36}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{product}<30)&=\\frac{11}{12}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "not a square",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{9}$\n\nSubtract the probability of the eight ordered outcomes giving square products from $1$.",
          "worked": "The square products possible are $1$, $4$, $9$, $16$, $25$ and $36$. They arise from the six doubles $(1,1)$ through $(6,6)$, together with $(1,4)$ and $(4,1)$: eight ordered outcomes out of $36$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{product is not a square})&=1-\\frac{8}{36}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{product is not a square})&=\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "not divisible by 10.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{5}{6}$\n\nSubtract the probability of rolling a $5$ and an even number, in either order, from $1$.",
          "worked": "A product divisible by $10$ requires a $5$ and one of $2$, $4$ or $6$. The ordered outcomes are $(5,2)$, $(2,5)$, $(5,4)$, $(4,5)$, $(5,6)$ and $(6,5)$: six out of $36$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{product is not divisible by }10)&=1-\\frac{6}{36}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{product is not divisible by }10)&=\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
